      "code_hash": "bae4e1178c71d8badda90194ac582461",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"verdict-reverted\">Verdict: reverted</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">qwen3_06b breached SLO (2934ms vs 1500ms); glm4_9b breached SLO (7753ms vs 6000ms)</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Memory fit was never the binding constraint</strong> \u2014 the fit check cleared with 76.2GB spare. Device-time contention was: <code>qwen3_06b</code>'s p95 inflated <strong>+271%</strong> beside <code>glm4_9b</code>, whose traffic is 50% prefill.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ulZA",
      "code_hash": "20d90018c8cc67191af504e76bdd5e16",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"the-control-arm\">The control arm</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Claiming the agents are better requires something to be better <em>than</em>. This\nsweeps the identical lever space, spends the identical budget, and passes the\nidentical gates \u2014 choosing randomly instead of by reasoning.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
